      "message": "The change looks correct in the handling of the EINTR state, but I\u0027d suggest a slightly different approach to the fix. Instead of resetting `rc` and proceeding with the increment, only incrementing `pos` when we make progress.\n\nSomething like:\n\n```\ndiff --git a/socket-handler.c b/socket-handler.c\nindex a957b3c..ac29b13 100644\n--- a/socket-handler.c\n+++ b/socket-handler.c\n@@ -145,7 +145,7 @@ static ssize_t send_all(struct client *client, void *buf, size_t len,\n                flags |\u003d MSG_DONTWAIT;\n        }\n \n-       for (pos \u003d 0; pos \u003c len; pos +\u003d rc) {\n+       for (pos \u003d 0; pos \u003c len;) {\n                rc \u003d send(fd, (char *)buf + pos, len - pos, flags);\n                if (rc \u003c 0) {\n                        if (!block \u0026\u0026\n@@ -163,6 +163,7 @@ static ssize_t send_all(struct client *client, void *buf, size_t len,\n                if (rc \u003d\u003d 0) {\n                        return -1;\n                }\n+               pos +\u003d rc;\n        }\n \n        return (ssize_t)pos;\n\n```\n\n\nif that makes it slightly more clear?\n\nThe CI failures look like effects of a compiler bump, no action required there.",
